{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-98066","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-162385","text":"Skill 01 — The Ten Protocols"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98068","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162386","text":"OS-001 through OS-010: what each protocol specifies, which product implements it, and the cognitive science behind it. Eight cognitive primitives plus two cross-cutting protocols (PRISM diagnostic, PULSE temporal)."}]}],"id":"blk-98067","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-98069","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-162387","text":"Overview"}]},{"id":"blk-98070","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162388","text":"OpenSentience publishes ten numbered protocols organized in two layers:"}]},{"id":"blk-98071","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98073","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162389","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive primitives (OS-001 — OS-008)"},{"id":"spn-162390","text":" — eight individual capabilities,"}]}],"id":"blk-98072","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98074","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162391","text":"each grounded in a cognitive science thread."}]},{"id":"blk-98075","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98077","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162392","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cross-cutting protocols (OS-009 PRISM, OS-010 PULSE)"},{"id":"spn-162393","text":" — two sibling"}]}],"id":"blk-98076","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98078","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162394","text":"protocols that sit above the cognitive primitives and above the [&] structural composition layer. PULSE declares how every loop in the ecosystem cycles, nests, and signals; PRISM measures how well those loops actually learn over time."}]},{"id":"blk-98079","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162395","text":"The protocols are independent specifications — they can be adopted individually or composed together. A system may publish a PULSE manifest without implementing any cognitive primitive, and PRISM can benchmark any PULSE-conforming system without bespoke per-system integration."}]},{"id":"blk-98080","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-162396","text":"OS-001: Continual Learning"}]},{"id":"blk-98081","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162397","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-162398","text":" Hippocampal consolidation (McClelland et al. 1995)"}]},{"id":"blk-98082","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162399","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-98083","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98085","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162400","text":"Three node types: episodic (events), semantic (facts), procedural (workflows)"}]}],"id":"blk-98084","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98087","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162401","text":"Typed, weighted edges between nodes"}]}],"id":"blk-98086","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98089","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162402","text":"Confidence scores with evidence-calibrated assignment"}]}],"id":"blk-98088","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98091","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162403","text":"Consolidation cycle: decay low-confidence nodes, prune stale entries,"}]}],"id":"blk-98090","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98092","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162404","text":"merge near-duplicates, strengthen co-retrieved edges"}]},{"id":"blk-98093","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98095","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162405","text":"Memory timescales: working memory (session), short-term (hours), long-term"}]}],"id":"blk-98094","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98096","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162406","text":"(persistent)"}]},{"id":"blk-98097","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162407","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-162408","text":" New memories must be stored quickly (hippocampal fast-write) without disrupting existing knowledge (neocortical slow-consolidation). This maps to immediate ETS/SQLite writes with background consolidation."}]},{"id":"blk-98098","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162409","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-162410","text":" Graphonomous ("},{"id":"spn-162411","marks":["code"],"text":"store_node"},{"id":"spn-162412","text":", "},{"id":"spn-162413","marks":["code"],"text":"store_edge"},{"id":"spn-162414","text":", "},{"id":"spn-162415","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-162416","text":", "},{"id":"spn-162417","marks":["code"],"text":"run_consolidation"},{"id":"spn-162418","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-98099","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-162419","text":"OS-002: Topological Routing (kappa)"}]},{"id":"blk-98100","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162420","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-162421","text":" Working memory gating (O'Reilly & Frank 2006)"}]},{"id":"blk-98101","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162422","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-98102","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98104","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162423","text":"The kappa parameter: a measure of cyclicity in a knowledge subgraph"}]}],"id":"blk-98103","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98106","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162424","text":"Strongly connected component (SCC) detection on retrieved neighborhoods"}]}],"id":"blk-98105","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98108","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162425","text":"Routing decision: kappa = 0 implies fast path (acyclic, no conflict),"}]}],"id":"blk-98107","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98109","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162426","text":"kappa > 0 implies deliberate path (cycles exist, may contain contradictions)"}]},{"id":"blk-98110","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98112","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162427","text":"Topological features: SCC count, max SCC size, edge density within cycles"}]}],"id":"blk-98111","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98113","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162428","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-162429","text":" The prefrontal cortex gates information into working memory based on relevance and conflict signals. Kappa serves as the conflict signal — cyclic knowledge regions indicate unresolved tension that requires deliberation before action."}]},{"id":"blk-98114","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162430","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-162431","text":" Graphonomous routing layer ("},{"id":"spn-162432","marks":["code"],"text":"topology_analyze"},{"id":"spn-162433","text":", "},{"id":"spn-162434","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-162435","text":" topology annotations)"}]},{"id":"blk-98115","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-162436","text":"OS-003: Deliberation Orchestrator"}]},{"id":"blk-98116","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162437","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-162438","text":" Dual-process theory (Kahneman 2011)"}]},{"id":"blk-98117","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162439","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-98118","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98120","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162440","text":"Four-phase deliberation: bid, debate, vote, commit"}]}],"id":"blk-98119","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98122","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162441","text":"Argumentation framework: claims, warrants, rebuttals"}]}],"id":"blk-98121","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98124","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162442","text":"Consensus mechanisms: majority, supermajority, unanimity"}]}],"id":"blk-98123","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98126","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162443","text":"Timeout and escalation policies"}]}],"id":"blk-98125","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98128","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162444","text":"Triggered when kappa routing indicates deliberation is needed"}]}],"id":"blk-98127","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98129","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162445","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-162446","text":" System 1 (fast, automatic) handles routine decisions. System 2 (slow, deliberate) engages when conflict is detected. The kappa threshold is the trigger that shifts from fast to deliberate processing."}]},{"id":"blk-98130","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162447","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-162448","text":" AgenTroMatic ("},{"id":"spn-162449","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate"},{"id":"spn-162450","text":" tool in Graphonomous provides the single-agent deliberation path)"}]},{"id":"blk-98131","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-162451","text":"OS-004: Attention Engine"}]},{"id":"blk-98132","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162452","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-162453","text":" Endogenous attention (Desimone & Duncan 1995)"}]},{"id":"blk-98133","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162454","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-98134","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98136","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162455","text":"Three-phase cycle: survey (scan environment), triage (rank by salience),"}]}],"id":"blk-98135","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98137","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162456","text":"dispatch (act on highest-priority items)"}]},{"id":"blk-98138","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98140","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162457","text":"Salience scoring: combines urgency, recency, goal relevance, and confidence"}]}],"id":"blk-98139","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98142","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162458","text":"Goal bias: active goals increase salience of related knowledge"}]}],"id":"blk-98141","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98144","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162459","text":"Dispatch modes: act (execute), learn (gather more context), escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-98143","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98145","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162460","text":"(request human intervention), idle (nothing needed)"}]},{"id":"blk-98146","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162461","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-162462","text":" Biological attention is goal-directed (endogenous) not just stimulus-driven (exogenous). The attention engine prioritizes based on the agent's active goals, not just what is new or loud."}]},{"id":"blk-98147","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162463","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-162464","text":" Graphonomous attention module ("},{"id":"spn-162465","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_survey"},{"id":"spn-162466","text":", "},{"id":"spn-162467","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_run_cycle"},{"id":"spn-162468","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-98148","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-162469","text":"OS-005: Model Tier Adaptation"}]},{"id":"blk-98149","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162470","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-162471","text":" Resource rationality (Lieder & Griffiths 2020)"}]},{"id":"blk-98150","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162472","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-98151","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98153","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162473","text":"Three tiers: "},{"id":"spn-162474","marks":["code"],"text":"local_small"},{"id":"spn-162475","text":" (8B parameter models), "},{"id":"spn-162476","marks":["code"],"text":"local_large"},{"id":"spn-162477","text":" (70B+),"}]}],"id":"blk-98152","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98154","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162478","marks":["code"],"text":"cloud_frontier"},{"id":"spn-162479","text":" (largest available)"}]},{"id":"blk-98155","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98157","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162480","text":"Same topology and tool surface at every tier — only depth and latency differ"}]}],"id":"blk-98156","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98159","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162481","text":"Escalation rules: when local_small confidence is below threshold, escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-98158","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98160","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162482","text":"to local_large; when local_large is insufficient, escalate to cloud_frontier"}]},{"id":"blk-98161","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98163","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162483","text":"Budget constraints: token limits, latency targets, cost caps per tier"}]}],"id":"blk-98162","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98164","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162484","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-162485","text":" Optimal cognition allocates computational resources proportional to decision importance. Simple decisions use fast/cheap processing; high-stakes decisions justify expensive computation."}]},{"id":"blk-98165","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162486","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-162487","text":" Graphonomous and Agentelic (tier selection and escalation logic)"}]},{"id":"blk-98166","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-162488","text":"OS-006: Agent Governance Shim"}]},{"id":"blk-98167","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162489","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-162490","text":" Executive function (Miyake et al. 2000)"}]},{"id":"blk-98168","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162491","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-98169","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98171","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162492","text":"Permission taxonomy: filesystem, network, tool_invocation, graph_access"}]}],"id":"blk-98170","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98173","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162493","text":"Lifecycle state machine: installed, enabled, running, disabled, removed"}]}],"id":"blk-98172","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98175","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162494","text":"Graduated autonomy: observe, advise, act"}]}],"id":"blk-98174","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162495","text":"Append-only audit trail with typed events"}]}],"id":"blk-98176","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98179","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162496","text":"OTP-native implementation: GenStateMachine, ETS, DynamicSupervisor"}]}],"id":"blk-98178","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98180","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162497","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-162498","text":" Executive function provides inhibitory control (permissions), task switching (lifecycle), and cognitive flexibility (autonomy levels). Without executive function, an agent cannot self-regulate — it either does nothing or does everything."}]},{"id":"blk-98181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162499","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-162500","text":" "},{"id":"spn-162501","marks":["code"],"text":"open_sentience"},{"id":"spn-162502","text":" hex package (this project)"}]},{"id":"blk-98182","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-162503","text":"OS-007: Adversarial Robustness"}]},{"id":"blk-98183","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162504","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-162505","text":" Immune system — self/non-self discrimination"}]},{"id":"blk-98184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162506","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-98185","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98187","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162507","text":"Five threat categories: prompt injection, model poisoning, side-channel,"}]}],"id":"blk-98186","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98188","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162508","text":"identity spoofing, resource exhaustion"}]},{"id":"blk-98189","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98191","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162509","text":"Detection rules per category"}]}],"id":"blk-98190","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98193","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162510","text":"Defense protocols: quarantine, circuit-break, escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-98192","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98195","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162511","text":"Integration with OS-006 for permission revocation and OS-008 for circuit"}]}],"id":"blk-98194","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162512","text":"breaking"}]},{"id":"blk-98197","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162513","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-162514","text":" OpenSentience security module (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-98198","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-162515","text":"OS-008: Agent Harness"}]},{"id":"blk-98199","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162516","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-162517","text":" Supervisory attentional system (Norman & Shallice 1986)"}]},{"id":"blk-98200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162518","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-98201","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98203","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162519","text":"Pipeline ordering enforcement (retrieve → route → act → learn)"}]}],"id":"blk-98202","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162520","text":"Quality gates between pipeline stages"}]}],"id":"blk-98204","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98207","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162521","text":"Sprint contracts: bounded execution with explicit goals and success criteria"}]}],"id":"blk-98206","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98209","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162522","text":"Context management: 60% threshold, compaction, Graphonomous overflow"}]}],"id":"blk-98208","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98211","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162523","text":"Generator-evaluator separation for adversarial grading"}]}],"id":"blk-98210","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98212","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162524","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-162525","text":" OpenSentience harness module (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-98213","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-162526","text":"OS-009: PRISM — Protocol for Rating Iterative System Memory"}]},{"id":"blk-98214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162527","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-162528","text":" Meta-cognition + psychometrics (Item Response Theory, signal detection theory)"}]},{"id":"blk-98215","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162529","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-98216","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98218","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162530","text":"9 continual-learning dimensions (retention, plasticity, transfer,"}]}],"id":"blk-98217","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-98219","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162531","text":"contradiction handling, etc.)"}]},{"id":"blk-98220","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-98222","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-162532","text":"4-phase evaluation loop: compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose"}]}],"id